{
  "title": "Frappe Learning \u2014 EdTech / Learning Management Systems (2,930\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: Frappe Learning\nDomain: EdTech / Learning Management Systems | Scale: medium | Stars: 2,930\nProblem: Provides an easy-to-use, open-source learning management system for creating and delivering online courses with structured content, live classes, and certification. Designed as a simpler alternative to complex platforms like Moodle.\nTarget users: Course creators, Educational institutions, Online learning platforms, Corporate training teams, Independent instructors\nCore features: Structured Learning (3-level hierarchy: courses, chapters, lessons); Live Classes with Zoom integration and batch grouping; Quizzes with multiple question types (single-choice, multiple-choice, open-ended); Assignments with PDF/document submission; Certificate generation with customizable templates; Learner batching and progress tracking; Role-based access control (instructors, learners, admins)\nIntegrations: Zoom (live classes), Frappe Framework ecosystem, Frappe UI components\nTech stack: Vue 3 with Frappe UI + Python with Frappe Framework + MariaDB (via Frappe Framework) + Docker, Frappe Cloud, self-hosted options\nKey libraries: Frappe Framework, Frappe UI, Cypress (testing), Vue\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Built on established Frappe ecosystem, leveraging a mature full-stack framework rather than building from scratch, reducing development complexity\n- Three-tier course hierarchy (courses \u2192 chapters \u2192 lessons) provides clear content organization and learner context\n- Integrated Zoom live classes directly within the platform streamlines the learning experience without external tool switching\n- Managed hosting option (Frappe Cloud) and straightforward self-hosting deployment scripts reduce barriers to production deployment",
